---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import NumberLineWorksheetEditor from '../components/NumberLineWorksheetEditor';
import { packIds, packs } from '../lib/number-line-worksheets';
import '../styles/coordinate.css';
import '../styles/worksheets.css';
const description =
  'Make free number line worksheets with 6, 9 or 12 questions. Practice negative numbers, fractions and jumps. Download A4 or Letter PDFs with separate answer keys.';
---

<Layout
  title="Number Line Worksheets — Free Generator & PDF Packs | ChartsAI"
  description={description}
  schema={[
    {
      '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
      name: 'Number line worksheet generator',
      applicationCategory: 'EducationalApplication',
      operatingSystem: 'Web browser',
      isAccessibleForFree: true,
      offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
      url: 'https://www.chartsai.com/number-line-worksheets/',
      featureList: [
        '6, 9 or 12 questions',
        'Negative integers, fractions and unit jumps',
        'A4 and US Letter PDF',
        'Separate answer pages',
        'CSV questions and answers',
      ],
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        {
          '@type': 'ListItem',
          position: 1,
          name: 'Math tools',
          item: 'https://www.chartsai.com/math-tools/',
        },
        {
          '@type': 'ListItem',
          position: 2,
          name: 'Number line worksheets',
          item: 'https://www.chartsai.com/number-line-worksheets/',
        },
      ],
    },
  ]}
>
  <section class="container coordinate-intro">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/math-tools/">Math tools</a><span>/</span><span>Number line worksheets</span>
    </nav><span class="eyebrow">FREE PRINTABLE PRACTICE · NO SIGNUP</span><h1>
      Number line<br /><em>worksheets.</em>
    </h1><p>
      Choose a skill. Get a fresh set of questions. Print a worksheet with space to work and a separate answer
      key. Practice negative numbers, fractions, or addition and subtraction on equally spaced number lines.
    </p><div class="worksheet-pack-links">
      <a href="#worksheet-generator">Make your worksheet ↓</a><a href="#ready-made-packs"
        >Download ready-made PDFs ↓</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="container">
    <NumberLineWorksheetEditor client:load /><noscript
      ><p>Use the ready-made PDF packs below. Enable JavaScript to generate a different set.</p></noscript
    >
  </div>
  <section class="container section coordinate-reference">
    <h2>From a topic to a printable lesson</h2><ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Choose a practice pack and question count.</strong> Use 6, 9 or 12 exercises. For integers and fractions,
        choose reading marked points, plotting given values, or both. Fraction steps can be halves, quarters, fifths
        or tenths.
      </li><li>
        <strong>Generate a fresh set when you need another version.</strong> Each set uses distinct exercise specifications;
        a value can recur on a different fraction window. Paper size and answer-key settings keep the questions
        unchanged.
      </li><li>
        <strong>Check the preview, then download.</strong> A4 and US Letter PDFs place three questions on each page.
        Answer pages follow all the question pages, so you can print or distribute them separately. Print at 100%
        scale.
      </li>
    </ol><p>
      For one custom diagram, decimal steps, blank lines or open and closed intervals, use the <a
        href="/number-line-generator/">number line generator</a
      >. This worksheet builder creates bounded practice sets; it does not accept arbitrary equations or grade
      student responses.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="container section" id="ready-made-packs">
    <span class="eyebrow">ORIGINAL PRACTICE PACKS · READY NOW</span><h2>Three ways to practice</h2><p>
      Each free pack includes six original questions and a matching answer key: two question pages followed by
      two answer pages. The fraction pack starts with quarters. These files work without JavaScript.
    </p><div class="worksheet-packs">
      {
        packIds.map((id) => (
          <article class="worksheet-pack" id={id}>
            <>
              <img
                src={`/worksheets/assets/${id}.svg`}
                width="800"
                height="1131"
                alt={`First question sheet: ${packs[id].title}`}
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <h3>{packs[id].title}</h3>
              <p>{packs[id].description}</p>
              <p>
                <strong>Try this:</strong> {packs[id].tip}
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Worked example:</strong> {packs[id].example}
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Watch for:</strong> {packs[id].mistake}
              </p>
              <div class="worksheet-pack-links">
                <>
                  <a href={`/worksheets/assets/${id}-a4.pdf`} download>
                    A4 PDF ↓
                  </a>
                  <a href={`/worksheets/assets/${id}-letter.pdf`} download>
                    Letter PDF ↓
                  </a>
                  <a href={`/worksheets/assets/${id}.csv`} download>
                    Questions & answers CSV ↓
                  </a>
                  <a href={`?pack=${id}#worksheet-generator`}>Customize this pack ↗</a>
                </>
              </div>
            </>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section coordinate-reference">
    <h2>How these worksheets are made</h2><p>
      The generator selects from a finite pool of valid exercises using a reproducible set number. Integer
      lines run from −10 to 10. Fraction lines span two units within 0–5, with equal fractional steps. Jumps
      use addition or subtraction of positive integers from 1 to 6, and both the starting value and answer
      remain between −10 and 10.
    </p><p>
      On reading questions, only the two endpoint values are labelled. Learners determine the step size from
      the spaces and identify point A. On plotting questions, every tick is labelled and learners place the
      given point. The key shows the point and its value. Fraction answers are simplified, so 2/4 appears as
      1/2; equivalent answers are valid.
    </p><p>
      Question and answer pages share the same number-line geometry used by the interactive diagram tool. The
      PDF uses high-resolution page images rather than selectable text. The CSV provides the questions and
      answers as text. Screen previews shrink to fit; the printed page is the intended working size.
    </p><h2>Questions about printing and practice</h2><h3>Can I download only the questions?</h3><p>
      Yes. Uncheck “Include separate answer pages” before downloading a generated PDF. The ready-made packs
      include both sections; print only pages 1–2 if you want their questions alone. Previewing an answer key
      never adds answers to the question sheets.
    </p><h3>Can I make another version of the same activity?</h3><p>
      Use “Generate fresh questions.” The topic, question count and fraction steps stay the same while the set
      changes. A new set may reuse some numbers, but each worksheet avoids duplicate exercises. Changing the
      paper size preserves the set.
    </p><h3>Which ages or grades are these for?</h3><p>
      Choose by the skill a learner is practicing. There is no grade-level certification or claim of
      curriculum alignment. An adult should review the preview for the learner's needs, especially negative
      values and fractions greater than one.
    </p><h3>Are these free for a class or home lesson?</h3><p>
      Yes. Download, print and share these original practice sheets for teaching or independent study. There
      is no account, watermark over the questions, or upload required. Worksheet generation runs in your
      browser.
    </p><div class="worksheet-callout">
      <h3>Ready for two dimensions?</h3><p>
        Try the <a href="/coordinate-plane-generator/">coordinate plane generator</a> for ordered pairs, then the
        <a href="/slope-calculator/">slope calculator</a> to connect two points with rise and run. Explore all <a
          href="/math-tools/">free math tools</a
        > or the <a href="/printables/">printable library</a>.
      </p>
    </div><p class="byline">
      Original worksheets and generator by <a href="https://www.supamakers.com/">SupaMakers</a> · Reviewed September
      8, 2026 · <a href="/source/">Public source and methods</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
